ist_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test that covers the reported case, the half-to-even cases, and negatives:\nNo pytest installed, so I ran the test cases and the existing split test directly:\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round()` rounds it down. On top of that, `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (`0.125 \u2192 0.12`), which doesn't match the \"half up\" promise in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the number into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, which gives `\"2.675\"`, the value the customer sees. It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and returns a float, so callers like `add_vat` don't change. Negative halves round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`).\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the cases directly with `python3`:\n- Before the fix: `2.675 \u2192 2.67`, `0.125 \u2192 0.12`, `1.005 \u2192 1.0`.\n- After the fix: `2.68`, `0.13`, `1.01`. `2.674` still gives `2.67`, and `-2.675` gives `-2.68`.\n- The existing `test_split` still passes, and `add_vat(10)` gives `12.0`.\n\nI added a regression test, `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering these cases. It hasn't been run under pytest yet.\n\n**Not changed:** `split()` has a related float bug: `int(total * 100)` cuts off decimals, so a total like `0.29` (which is `28.999\u2026` when multiplied by 100) loses a cent. You didn't ask about it, so I didn't touch it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 248849, "requests_cache_write": 12665, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1595348, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2318, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither